What are the "two meanings" in terms of example sentences and their english
translations (or pseudo-english translations involving phrases like
"relative to the main selbri" etc...)

I originally thought that {vi} and friends were just like {ca} such that {mi
tcidu vi lo tricu} would be understood as "I read [short-distance-from] a
tree" and if I had used {vu} instead it would have been "I read
[long-distance-from] a tree".  A while back though, I was corrected by
someone or other that I want {bu'u} and friends for that sort of thing and
that my original sentence actually means something else (what it means I
don't remember any more).  .ija'ebo I don't use VI/ZI/etc.. any more as
tags.  How SHOULD I be using them (given either school of thought that
selkik was talking about)

